# Coturn / TURN for JobPilot interview rooms

Interview room WebRTC falls back to a public STUN server. For production NAT traversal, provide TURN credentials.

## Environment

```bash
# Optional STUN override (comma-separated)
STUN_URIS=stun:stun.l.google.com:19302

# Required for production-ready peer audio behind strict NATs
TURN_URIS=turn:turn.example.com:3478?transport=udp,turns:turn.example.com:5349?transport=tcp
TURN_USERNAME=jobpilot
TURN_CREDENTIAL=replace-me
```

JobPilot reads these in `resolveIceServers()` and returns them from `/api/room/:code/rtc`.

## Minimal coturn sketch

```
listening-port=3478
fingerprint
lt-cred-mech
user=jobpilot:replace-me
realm=turn.example.com
no-multicast-peers
no-cli
```

Use TLS (`turns:`) and firewall rules appropriate for your host. Rotate credentials regularly.
